{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Turned aside</b> — Evil has come upon them, for their drinkers [סבאם] lack new wine, and they have not turned back from their evil way; rather, their kings say to others, for the sake of gifts: 'Give.' And the word הבו comes like את אשר תאפו אפו, and the essence is אפו, also אהבו." "<b>Give</b> — Also הבו לכם in all [cases], like רדו, צאו. And the variation in it is because of the guttural letter." "<b>Her shields</b> — These are the kings, like כי לה' מגיני ארץ. And the end of the verse proves it, for the meaning is doubled." "<b>And her shields</b> — belongs to 'House of Aven.'"], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:50:10.126918532Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}